SUMMARY:FreeOnFriday? Cabin Fever 23R
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\nRIDE LEADER: Jan Zerfoss\
 , average pace 12 mph.\nCue and Ride with GPS link: [Cabin Fever](https://
 ridewithgps.com/routes/40245570)\n**Be Safe\, Have Fun\, and Ride Together
 **\n\nThis is a casual ride and the ride leader will ride at the advertise
 d pace. Some riders may ride faster than the leader so we'll likely break 
 into one or more smaller groups. We will stop to regroup periodically. Ple
 ase stay with other riders in your pace group so everyone has someone to r
 ide with and nobody is riding solo. Usually no designated sweep but nobody
  will get dropped.\n\nTerre Hill Park has well maintained restrooms that a
 re usually open. There is also a bike repair station there.\n\nPost-ride c
 offee/refreshments - [Terre Hill Restaurant](http://www.terrehillrestauran
 t.com) Some of us may ride to the restaurant after the ride\; it is only a
 bout .25 mile from the parking lt.\n\nHelmets are mandatory. No earbuds. P
 lease bring water and a basic repair kit (spare tube\, tire levers\, pump/
 CO2 inflator).\n\nTo eliminate passing around a pen and paper waiver\, we 
 require LBC Club membership and Meetup RSVP below to join this ride. Being
  on\nMeetup does not mean you are a club member. Join here [Member Signup]
 (https://www.lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=60&club_id=257148)
 \n\nYour RSVP is your agreement to abide by the club's Code of Conduct: [C
 ode of Conduct](https://www.lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=22&
 club_id=257148&module_id=323984)\n\nGuidance if an incident occurs: [Incid
 ent Actions](https://lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id
 =257148&module_id=326137)
